{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27289374","formula":"C₆H₈CaO₈","hill":"C6H8CaO8","elements":["H","C","O","Ca"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":8.0,"O":8.0,"Ca":1.0},"names":{"en":"Calcium saccharate","uk":"Сахарат кальцію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Calcium D-glucarate (or calcium saccharate) is the calcium salt of D-glucaric acid (saccharic acid), a substance naturally found in small amounts in fruits and vegetables such as oranges, apples, grapefruits, and cruciferous vegetables. It is commonly used as a dietary supplement, primarily marketed for its potential role in supporting detoxification processes and hormone regulation. Preclinical studies suggest that calcium D-glucarate may possess anticarcinogenic properties and improve detoxification markers, but more definitive clinical research such as a randomized controlled trial is needed to verify health claims."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":154911,"mass":248.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"[C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H](C(=O)[O-])O)O)([C@H](C(=O)[O-])O)O.[Ca+2]","inchikey":"UGZVNIRNPPEDHM-SBBOJQDXSA-L","iupac":"calcium (2S,3S,4S,5R)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydroxyhexanedioate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"154911","atoms":23,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.024,"y":-0.22,"z":-0.228,"el":"C"},{"x":0.432,"y":0.268,"z":0.012,"el":"C"},{"x":1.433,"y":-0.893,"z":0.159,"el":"C"},{"x":2.862,"y":-0.348,"z":0.483,"el":"C"},{"x":3.237,"y":0.681,"z":-0.151,"el":"O"},{"x":3.484,"y":-1.03,"z":1.359,"el":"O"},{"x":1.054,"y":-1.806,"z":1.222,"el":"O"},{"x":0.825,"y":1.13,"z":-1.079,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.014,"y":0.958,"z":-0.32,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.347,"y":0.651,"z":0.424,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.372,"y":0.715,"z":-0.333,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.283,"y":0.449,"z":1.667,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.318,"y":1.269,"z":-1.719,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.072,"y":-0.949,"z":-1.48